description:
FILED s533c (Opus, 2026-11-05), found by the review of s533c's wide emission A/B (t/mro/package_aliases.t:406 `local *Fooo:: = \%Baro::;`), PRE-EXISTING (main 0f2db817 prints the same as the tree).

REPRODUCER (scratch/s533c/p/stg.pl):
  package Baro; our $v = "baro-v"; sub hello { "baro hello" }
  package A::B; our $w = "ab-w";
  package main;
  {
    local *Fooo:: = \%Baro::;
    print exists $Fooo::{hello} ? "in: has hello\n" : "in: no hello\n";
    print defined(${"Fooo::v"}) ? "in: v=${'Fooo::v'}\n" : "in: v undef\n";
  }
  print exists $Fooo::{hello} ? "out: has hello\n" : "out: no hello\n";
  { local *A::C:: = \%A::B::; print exists $A::C::{w} ? "in2: has w\n" : "in2: no w\n"; }
perl 5.40.3: in: has hello / in: v=baro-v / out: no hello / in2: has w
PCL (0f2db817 and s533c alike): in: no hello / in: v undef / out: no hello / in2: no w  (SILENT WRONG)

MECHANISM (read, not fixed): the unlocalized `*Fooo:: = \%Baro::` compiles to `(p-setf (p-stash "Fooo") (p-backslash (p-stash "Baro")))` -- the stash-alias path of #3321 (`*p-stash-aliases*`).  The LOCALIZED spelling is `(p-local-glob "main" "Fooo::" RHS …)`, the ordinary glob localizer, which saves / clears / assigns the four slot symbols of a glob named `Fooo::` in main -- it never reaches the stash-alias record, so nothing aliases and nothing is restored.  (Until s533c the static glob name of `*Fooo::` came out right only by a stale `$1` in v1's parser; s533c reads a stash glob `*Pkg::` / `*A::B::` explicitly -- ("main" "Fooo::"), ("A" "C::").)

FIX SKETCH: a `local` of a STASH glob (static name ending in `::`) with a stash / stash-ref value lowers to a localized stash alias: record A -> B in *p-stash-aliases* (and the stash memo) for the dynamic extent, restore the previous entry on exit -- the same record #3321's p-stash-assign writes.
